{"input":{"file_path":"/home/sandbox/.claude/projects/-workspace/memory/rct2-coaster-contest-tuning.md"},"kind":"tool","name":"Read","output":"1\t---\n2\tname: rct2-coaster-contest-tuning\n3\tdescription: Hard-won tuning facts for the RCT2 steel-twister (ride_type 51) coaster-design contest via the coaster MCP tools\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 7263586d-30ff-4ca5-831b-323955bcf1c3\n8\t  modified: 2026-07-25T14:21:16.517Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tRound-by-round results in the coaster MCP contest (steel twister, ride_type 51): scores plateau at\n12\texcitement 6.8-7.0 for lift-hill + loops + airtime layouts. Round 3: 6.99 (int 9.94). Round 4 best: 6.93\n13\t(int 9.96, 5 inversions, 744 length, 57 airtime, 100 pieces).\n14\t\n15\tFacts established by experiment (2026-07-25, round 4):\n16\t- **Intensity >= 10 halves excitement, repeatedly.** A build with strictly better raw stats\n17\t  (airtime 82, 14 drops, 6 inversions, length 874) scored 1.66 because intensity hit 15.3.\n18\t  Staying just under 10.0 is the single most important constraint.\n19\t- Adding elements (loops, hops, length) raises intensity much faster than excitement; going from\n20\t  int 7.09 -> 9.96 moved excitement only 6.86 -> 6.93.\n21\t- Lowering the lift 48z and softening the first drop (one down_60 instead of two) did NOT cut\n22\t  intensity meaningfully (15.7 vs 15.3) — element/turn COUNT drives it, not just peak G.\n23\t- **A corkscrew_up + corkscrew_down pair counts as only 1 inversion**; each vertical_loop counts as 1.\n24\t- max_lateral_g ~3.0 recurs from banked_*_turn_5 taken at speed; tight banked_*_turn_3 near ground\n25\t  pushed it to 3.04+ and spiked intensity.\n26\t- Geometry: cursor deltas rotate by (x,y)->(y,-x) per dir increment (dir 0=-x,1=+y,2=+x,3=-y), so\n27\t  dir-0 piece_geometry plus that rotation predicts everything; closure can be planned fully on paper.\n28\t- Circuit closes when the cursor returns to the start tile with the start dir and z, i.e. the final\n29\t  approach must run in along the station row from behind the begin_station tile.\n30\t- Similarity stayed ~0.35 (safe, penalty starts at 0.5) with 2-lift and 4-loop original layouts.\n31\t\n32\t**Next round hypothesis to test:** build FEWER, gentler elements to land intensity ~8.5-9.5 while\n33\tkeeping length/airtime high (long shallow airtime hills, no down_60, banked turns only at low speed),\n34\tsince excitement per intensity point is what is capped.\n35\t","seq":2,"status":"completed"}
