{"input":{"content":"---\nname: rct2-coaster-contest-tuning\ndescription: Hard-won tuning facts for the RCT2 steel-twister (ride_type 51) coaster-design contest via the coaster MCP tools\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 7263586d-30ff-4ca5-831b-323955bcf1c3\n  modified: 2026-07-25T00:00:00.000Z\n---\n\nRound-by-round results in the coaster MCP contest (steel twister, ride_type 51): scores plateau at\nexcitement 6.7-7.0. R3: 6.99 (int 9.94). R4: 6.93 (int 9.96, 5 inv). R5: 6.84 (int 9.58, 4 inv,\nlength 707, airtime 64, 11 drops, 100 pieces).\n\nFacts established by experiment:\n- **Intensity >= 10 halves excitement, repeatedly.** Stay just under 10.0; it is the binding constraint.\n- **Lift height / first-drop depth is the dominant intensity driver.** R5 A/B on an otherwise IDENTICAL\n  layout: 15 up_25 chain (top z=368, drop 24 steps) -> int 9.19 / exc 6.71; 17 up_25 (top z=400, drop\n  30 steps) -> int 14.3 / exc 2.10. Never exceed ~24 height-steps of first drop. Two down_60 in the\n  drop is also too much; one is right.\n- Adding one vertical loop to a fixed layout: int +0.4, exc +0.13 (6.71/9.19 -> 6.84/9.58). Good trade.\n- Adding one low airtime hill (airtime 64->76, 12 drops): exc -0.03, int +0.1. Airtime/drops are\n  NOT worth much on their own; inversions and drop height are.\n- A corkscrew_up + corkscrew_down pair = 1 inversion; each vertical_loop = 1.\n- max_lateral_g pins at 3.0 from banked_*_turn_5/3 at speed regardless of tweaks.\n- **Half-loop pair (half_loop_up + half_loop_down) shifts z by a net -8**, which breaks the mod-16\n  z lattice (every flat->flat climb/descent is a multiple of 16). Use an even number of half-loop\n  pairs, or place one so the -8 lands exactly at station level. Untested for score.\n\nGeometry / planning (fully solved, closure can be done on paper):\n- Cursor deltas rotate (x,y)->(y,-x) per dir increment (0=-x,1=+y,2=+x,3=-y); dir-0 piece_geometry\n  plus that rotation predicts everything.\n- U-turn nets: turn_5 pair = 5 tiles of lateral shift, turn_3 pair = 3, plus 1 tile along travel.\n  right_helix_*_large is a 180 U-turn with dy=5, dz=+-16.\n- vertical_loop shifts y by -+1 (left/right); fix with an s_bend to keep rows aligned.\n- Circuit closes when the cursor returns to the begin_station tile with the start dir and z, i.e. the\n  return leg runs in along the station row from behind it.\n- Similarity stays ~0.37-0.40 (safe; penalty starts at 0.5) with lift + 3-4 loops + corkscrew layouts.\n\n**Next round: the 6.7-7.0 plateau is real.** Try qualitatively different levers instead of more\nelements: a second chain lift mid-circuit (regains height without a deeper single drop), helices for\nlength, or a longer/lower layout with 5-6 inversions at drop <= 24 steps.\n","file_path":"/home/sandbox/.claude/projects/-workspace/memory/rct2-coaster-contest-tuning.md"},"kind":"tool","name":"Write","output":"The file /home/sandbox/.claude/projects/-workspace/memory/rct2-coaster-contest-tuning.md has been updated successfully.","seq":34,"status":"completed"}
{"kind":"text","seq":35,"text":"Round complete. Four tested builds; best banked at **6.84**.\n\nWhat the round established (three builds on an otherwise identical layout isolated the variable):\n\n| build | lift | drop | inversions | intensity | excitement |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| v1 | 15×up_25 | 24 steps | 3 | 9.19 | 6.71 |\n| v2 | 17×up_25 | 30 steps | 4 | **14.30** | 2.10 |\n| v3 | 15×up_25 | 24 steps | 4 | 9.58 | **6.84** |\n| v4 | v3 + airtime hill | 24 steps | 4 | 9.68 | 6.81 |\n\nFirst-drop depth is the dominant intensity driver — six extra height-steps took intensity from 9.19 to 14.3 and gutted excitement. Adding a vertical loop was the good trade (+0.4 intensity, +0.13 excitement); adding an airtime hill was not (+12 airtime, −0.03 excitement). Similarity stayed at 0.37, well under the 0.5 penalty threshold. Memory updated with the A/B numbers and the half-loop mod-16 z-lattice gotcha for round 6.\n\n**Best coaster: a 100-piece steel twister — 24-step drop with a single down_60, three vertical loops, a corkscrew pair, four airtime hills and two banked U-turns — excitement 6.84 at intensity 9.58, no crash.**"}
